*(
    title: Central Banks
    description: How the Reserve Bank of Australia moves one overnight interest rate, and why that reaches every price in the economy.
    tags: central banks, monetary policy, reserve bank of australia, cash rate, inflation targeting
    lesson
)

// Every RBA cash rate target change from June 2019 to the August 2026 meeting.
// The date is the day each decision took effect, written ISO so the axis places
// it at its fractional year. The final row is the 12 Aug 2026 meeting, a hold,
// so the staircase runs to the present.
@data#cash{
    date       | target
    2019-06-05 | 1.25
    2019-07-03 | 1.00
    2019-10-02 | 0.75
    2020-03-04 | 0.50
    2020-03-20 | 0.25
    2020-11-04 | 0.10
    2022-05-04 | 0.35
    2022-06-08 | 0.85
    2022-07-06 | 1.35
    2022-08-03 | 1.85
    2022-09-07 | 2.35
    2022-10-05 | 2.60
    2022-11-02 | 2.85
    2022-12-07 | 3.10
    2023-02-08 | 3.35
    2023-03-08 | 3.60
    2023-05-03 | 3.85
    2023-06-07 | 4.10
    2023-11-08 | 4.35
    2025-02-19 | 4.10
    2025-05-21 | 3.85
    2025-08-13 | 3.60
    2026-02-04 | 3.85
    2026-03-18 | 4.10
    2026-05-06 | 4.35
    2026-08-12 | 4.35
}

// Annual CPI inflation, all groups, Australia. Readings to the September 2025
// quarter are quarterly and are dated at the end of their quarter; the ABS moved
// to a complete monthly CPI from November 2025, so later readings are monthly.
@data#cpi{
    date       | rate
    2024-12-31 | 2.4
    2025-03-31 | 2.4
    2025-06-30 | 2.1
    2025-09-30 | 3.2
    2025-10-31 | 3.8
    2026-03-31 | 4.6
    2026-06-30 | 3.8
    2026-07-31 | 3.5
}

